<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martti Rautanen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a>–<a href="/years/1926">1926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Nakambale</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martti Rautanen was a Finnish Lutheran missionary who worked among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovambo-people">Ovambo</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> from 1870 until his death in 1926. Based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olukonda">Olukonda</a> in Ondonga, where he was known as Nakambale, he translated the Bible and other texts into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndonga-dialect">Oshindonga</a>, founded the first congregations and helped make Ondonga largely Christian. He also collected plants and wrote on Ovambo customs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martti-rautanen.jpg" alt="Martti Rautanen" width="320" height="531" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rautanen1868.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Finnish Lutheran missionaries arrived in 1870, and <b>Martti Rautanen</b> worked at Olukonda, translating the Bible into Oshindonga.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-ondonga">Kingdom of Ondonga</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Tikopis, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=59.4,28.7&amp;year=1897" aria-label="Tikopis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5154 168 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Martti Rautanen"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5604 438h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5604 438h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=59.4,28.7&amp;year=1897">What was here in 1897? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
